<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Andriamasinavalona</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 1675–<a href="/years/1710">1710</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Andriamasinavalona was a king of Imerina in the central highlands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a> who ruled around 1675–1710. He extended the kingdom to its largest size before the nineteenth century but divided it among his sons, leading to nearly a century of rivalry and war between four Merina kingdoms. The realm was reunited only by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andrianampoinimerina">Andrianampoinimerina</a> at the end of the eighteenth century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/andriamasinavalona.jpg" alt="Andriamasinavalona" width="320" height="366" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ny Maraina Randrianarisoa - Tanora taranak'Andriamasinavalona · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Andriamasinavalona_2.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
